-- title:
--   Index of Γ∩ sΓ s⁻¹ equals the degeneracy degree
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_2,b_2$, a nonzero squarefree $N$ and primes $q,q'$ with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$, $q'\neq q$ and $q,q'\ge 5$. Assume $a_2<0$, $b_2<0$ and that for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_2,b_2]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q\in v$. Let $\Lambda_2$ be a maximal order (an order not properly contained in any order) and $R_2\le\Lambda_2$ an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders of relative additive index $N$ in the first. Let $n_2$ lie in `primeHeckeSet R₂ q'` (the adelic unit and $q'$ times its inverse lie in the finite adele box of $R_2$, while its inverse and $q'^{-1}$ times it do not), and assume `meetOrder R₂ n₂` $=R_2\cap n_2R_2n_2^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nq'$; let $v_1$ be a height-one prime containing $q'$. Let $\ell$ be a prime distinct from $q$ and $q'$, $s$ a unit of the quaternion algebra with $\mathrm{nrd}(s)=\ell$, and $s_f$ an adelic unit whose component at each $u$ not containing $q'$ is $s\otimes 1$ and whose component at each $u$ containing $q'$ is $1$, such that the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ times $s_f^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₂ (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ (members of the $\ell$-Hecke set of `meetOrder R₂ n₂` which do not normalise that order and do not conjugate $\Lambda_2$ to an order containing it) and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` otherwise. Let $\Gamma$ be the subgroup of units $x$ characterised by: $x$ lies in `awayUnits R₂ v₁`, i.e. for every height-one prime $w\neq v_1$ the image of $x$ in $(\mathrm{Loc}\,a_2\,b_2\,w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_2$ at $w$, and $\mathrm{padicValRat}_{q'}(\mathrm{nrd}(x))$ is even. Then the relative index of $\Gamma\cap s\Gamma s^{-1}$ in $\Gamma$ equals `HeckeTower.arrowDegree N (ℓ,0)`, namely $\ell$ if $\ell\mid N$ and $\ell+1$ otherwise.
--
--   This computes the local index attached to an $\ell$-degeneracy arrow of the Hecke tower on the definite quaternionic side ramified at $q$ and $\infty$, matching it with the expected degree $\ell$ or $\ell+1$ according to whether $\ell$ divides the level. It is used by the statements that build the descent intertwining data and the orbit/stabiliser finiteness input for the arrow labelled $(\ell,0)$.
